   "posted": "2026-11-20",
   "expires": "2027-01-01",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<strong>About The Role</strong><p>FDM is a global business and technology consultancy seeking a Mid-Level Full-Stack Engineer – .NET / Optimizely CMS to work for our client within the public sector. This is initially a 6- week contract with the potential to extend and will be a remote role </p><p><br></p><p>We are looking for two Mid-Level Full-Stack Engineers to support the development and modernisation of an existing digital platform.</p><p><br></p><p>The successful engineers will have strong C#/.NET and ASP.NET Core experience alongside working knowledge of Optimizely CMS. The roles will involve converting and modernising existing controllers, views and components, rebuilding integrations, and developing automated tests.</p><p><br></p><p>Ideally, one engineer will have a primary focus on the website, while the second will focus on the portal.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Develop and maintain full-stack applications using C#, .NET and ASP.NET Core.</li><li>Work with Optimizely CMS, including content types, blocks, visitor groups and multi-site functionality.</li><li>Convert and modernise existing controllers, views and reusable components.</li><li>Rebuild and enhance existing system and third-party integrations.</li><li>Develop high-quality, maintainable and reusable code.</li><li>Create and maintain automated tests to support application quality and reliability.</li><li>Troubleshoot issues across both front-end and back-end components.</li><li>Work within an established codebase and contribute to ongoing platform improvements.</li><li>Collaborate with the wider engineering and delivery teams throughout development and release cycles.</li></ul><strong>About You</strong><p><br></p><ul><li>Strong commercial experience with C# and .NET.</li><li>Solid experience developing applications with ASP.NET Core.</li><li>Full-stack development experience across both front-end and back-end technologies.</li><li>Working knowledge of Optimizely CMS.</li><li>Experience with Optimizely features such as:</li><li>Content types</li><li>Blocks</li><li>Visitor groups</li><li>Multi-site setups</li><li>Experience converting or refactoring existing controllers, views and components.</li><li>Experience building or rebuilding application integrations.</li><li>Strong understanding of automated testing and modern software engineering practices.</li><li>Ability to quickly understand and work effectively within an existing codebase.</li></ul><strong>About Us</strong><p>FDM is an award-winning global leader in tech and business talent solutions, backed by more than 35 years of industry experience. We have centres across Europe, North America, and Asia-Pacific, and a global workforce of over 2500 employees. FDM has shown exponential growth throughout the years, firmly establishing itself as an award-winning employer, currently listed on the FTSE4Good Index and as a 2026 Financial Times UK ‘Best Employer’. </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Diversity and Inclusion</strong></p><p><br></p><p>FDM Group is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, veteran status or any other status protected by federal, provincial or local laws.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Why join us</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Career coaching, mentoring and access to upskilling throughout your entire FDM career</li><li>Assignments with global companies and opportunities to work abroad</li><li>Opportunity to re-skill and up-skill into new areas, develop non-linear career paths and build a skillset within your field</li><li>Annual leave and work-place pension</li></ul><p><br></p>",
   "sponsorship": "not mentioned",
   "source": "Reed.co.uk",
