   "description": "<p><strong>Ready to Rise to the Top as a Quality Assurance Advisor</strong></p> <p>This is a fantastic opportunity for someone with quality management and auditing experience who is passionate about food safety, quality standards and continuous improvement. </p> <p>This role will be based at our Severnside site, located in Stonehouse Gloucestershire. </p> <p><strong>How You’ll Make an Impact </strong></p> <p>Reporting to the Technical Manager, you'll play a key role in maintaining and developing our Quality Management System (QMS), ensuring products consistently meet the highest standards while supporting operational excellence across the site. </p> <p>You'll work closely with production teams, suppliers and customers, helping to drive quality performance and best practice throughout the business. </p> <p>Other duties will include: </p> <ul> <li> <p>Supporting quality investigations and root cause analysis. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Coordinating internal and external audits. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Supporting operational teams to deliver quality and food safety standards. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Driving continuous improvement and Operational Excellence initiatives. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Building effective relationships with customers, suppliers and stakeholders. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Promoting health and safety best practice across the site. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Supporting the training and development of colleagues. </p> </li></ul> <p><strong>What You’ll Bring </strong></p> <p>You’ll be able to combine technical expertise with strong communication and organisational skills. </p> <p>You'll ideally have: </p> <ul> <li> <p>HACCP / Food safety qualification or equivalent </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>experience working within a food manufacturing, FMCG or regulated production environment </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>knowledge and experience of Quality Management Systems and quality assurance processes </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>an audit qualification (BRC), customer audits or experience participating in internal and external audits </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>understanding of Operational Excellence principles and continuous improvement methodologies </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>strong problem-solving and analytical skills and the ability to meet deadlines </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>excellent communication and stakeholder management abilities </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>the ability to influence and collaborate effectively at all levels of the business. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>confidence using Microsoft Office and other IT systems </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>a proactive, team-focused approach with a commitment to delivering high standards. </p> </li></ul> <p>Technical skills are important, but so is how you work. We're looking for people who bring our Muller Milk & Ingredients behaviours to life every day: </p> <p><strong>Be Bold | Own It | We Care | One Team </strong></p> <p><strong>No Hard Graft Goes Unnoticed </strong></p> <p>We're proud to recognise the contribution our people make through a competitive reward package including: </p> <ul> <li> <p>Contributory pension plan. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Generous annual leave. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Employee Assistance Programme. </p> </li></ul> <ul> <li> <p>Access to a Rewards Benefits Programme with discounts at over 800 retailers. </p> </li></ul> <p>Pour in the passion. Love the result. </p> <p>With training the support and freedom to own your growth, you can build your skills and shape your career here. Every day, we bring something different. </p> <p>Interested in learning more? We’d love to hear from you. We look forward to receiving your application, and the sooner the better. For any informal queries, please contact Mike Brett on . </p> <p>We want every candidate to have the opportunity to shine. Please let us know if there’s anything we can do to support you through the recruitment process. </p> <p><strong>United by Dairy, Powered by People </strong></p> <p>At Müller, everyone plays a part in creating the products the nation loves. </p> <p>Our mission is to deliver a better dairy future, and to put a smile on the nation's face. We have ambitious plans to put a Müller product in every fridge. That starts with our people. </p> <p>From farm to factory to fridge, our people help us work towards a more sustainable dairy industry. We value respect and honesty, embrace different skills and perspectives, and welcome the diversity of ideas needed to deliver the highest quality products. </p> <p>We are a household name, but we feel like a close community who comes together to spread greatness. And greatness is about more than just the products we make; it's about working together and knowing that your contribution matters. </p> <p>Together, we are building a better business from the inside out. </p> <p><strong>You can find out more about Müller and what it’s like to work for us by clicking here Careers at Müller UK & Ireland</strong></p>",
