   "description": "<p><strong>We are looking for an Optical Assistant to join the lovely Kings Lynn team working 4 days per week. Ideally, we would like you to be based in the Dereham/Norwich/Swaffham areas which will make it easier to cover the whole of the business patch.</strong></p> <p>Are you an experienced Optical Assistant, looking for more clinical exposure, with the addition of having more one-to-one time with patients? Then, look no further.</p> <p>What does the opportunity look like for you?</p> <p><strong>Starting and Benefits:</strong></p> <ul> <li>£25,174.50 per annum pro rata for 4 days plus great bonus scheme</li><li>Car allowance of £3,000 per annum</li><li>Monday to Friday working week, 37.5 hours</li><li>Excellent, achievable monthly bonus scheme</li><li>20 days holiday per annum plus 8 bank holidays per annum</li><li>Birthday day off </li><li>Access to specsavers perks</li><li>Excellent opportunity for career development with full support from the Directors</li></ul> <p><strong>What we would like from you:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Minimum of 12 months optical experience</li><li>Confident driver with full UK driving licence.</li><li>Happy to cover the Norfolk/Thetford, Fakenham and surrounding areas</li><li>Ability to confidently dispense SV, VF and BF </li><li>A confident and compassionate approach when dealing with patients</li></ul> <p><strong>A Little Bit About Specsavers Home Visits:</strong></p> <p>Specsavers Home Visits provides eye care to customers in their own homes. Our passion is to deliver outstanding customer care, expert eye care advice and product recommendations that best suit individual customer needs. Whether you are an Optical Assistant or Optometrist, our roles are highly rewarding with variation and flexibility providing a great work life balance. At Specsavers Home Visits you will be supported by a highly experienced professional team and have the opportunity for personal development and career progression. Our expectation is that you will share our vision to provide our patients with the very best professional service as well as exceptional customer care on every Home Visit.</p> <p>If are an experienced OA looking for a change from the high street and want more diversity and freedom in your working day, then this role could be perfect for you. It will allow you the opportunity to put your skills to the test and make a real difference to the quality of a person's life and help and support your local community. </p> <p>#LI-LH1 </p>",
