   "description": "<p>Job Title: Secure Care Worker <br><strong>Location:</strong> St Helens, Merseyside<br><strong>Hours:</strong> 38 hours per week<br><strong>Salary:</strong> £27,734.56 - £29,547.08 per annum</p> <p><strong>Are you passionate about making a difference in the lives of young people?</strong><br>Do you have a genuine interest in helping children and teens, even if you have no prior experience? If you're caring, compassionate, and ready to embark on a meaningful career, we want to hear from you!</p> <p>We're looking for individuals with a passion for working with young people to join our team as <strong>Secure Care Workers</strong> in our Secure Children's Home. No formal experience is required, just a drive to support and inspire young people who may be facing difficult challenges. We'll provide all the training and support you need to succeed.</p> <p><strong>The Role:</strong></p> <p>As a Secure Care Worker, you will be a vital part of a dedicated team, helping young people aged 10 to 17 find stability and hope during difficult times. You'll be providing hands-on care and support, engaging with them in day-to-day activities, education, and health-related matters. You'll also have the chance to focus on <strong>either 'intervention work' or 'activity work'</strong>, depending on your interests and strengths.</p> <p>Your role will involve:</p> <ul> <li>Offering care and emotional support to young people in a secure environment</li><li>Helping them build self-confidence and develop life skills</li><li>Supporting their education, health, and independence</li><li>Being a positive role model, making a lasting impact on their lives</li></ul> <p>No two days are the same in this role, and you'll need to be ready for a challenge. Our young people are unique individuals, and we're looking for someone who will treat them as such.</p> <p><strong>What We're Looking For:</strong></p> <ul> <li>A genuine passion for working with young people</li><li>An optimistic, caring, and compassionate attitude</li><li>A commitment to making a positive impact, no matter how small</li></ul> <p>If you're enthusiastic about working with children and teens and ready to take on a rewarding role, this could be the perfect opportunity for you - experience isn't necessary, just the right mindset!</p> <p><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Comprehensive training</strong> and a supportive induction programme to help you thrive</li><li>Group Personal Pension Scheme</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
