   "description": "<p><b>Children's Residential Support Worker - Complex Needs</b></p> <p><strong>Location:</strong> Northampton (NN1)<br><strong>Pay:</strong> £14.00 per hour<br><strong>Contract:</strong> Ongoing Agency Work<br><strong>Shifts:</strong> 12-hour Days (8am-8pm) & Waking Nights (8pm-8am)</p> <p>We are recruiting experienced <strong>Children's Residential Support Workers</strong> to support children and young people within a specialist semi-independent residential service. Support is provided on a <strong>1:1, 2:1 and 3:1 basis</strong> for young people with complex needs including <strong>Autism, ADHD, EBD, trauma, attachment difficulties, PDA, ODD, anxiety, self-harm, and behaviours that challenge</strong>.</p> <p><b>Key Responsibilities</b></p> <ul> <li>Provide therapeutic, person-centred support.</li><li>Support young people with daily routines, activities and independence.</li><li>Manage behaviours that challenge using trauma-informed approaches.</li><li>Follow care plans, risk assessments and behaviour support plans.</li><li>Administer medication where required.</li><li>Complete accurate records and reports.</li><li>Maintain safeguarding and child welfare standards.</li></ul> <p><b>Requirements</b></p> <ul> <li><strong>Level 3 Diploma/NVQ in Residential Childcare (or equivalent).</strong></li><li>Previous children's residential care experience.</li><li>Experience supporting young people with complex needs, Autism and ADHD.</li><li>Understanding of trauma, attachment and safeguarding.</li><li>Ability to work day and/or waking night shifts.</li></ul> <p><b>Desirable</b></p> <ul> <li>Physical Intervention/Restraint Training.</li><li>Knowledge of PACE, DDP, PDA, ODD and therapeutic care approaches.</li></ul> <p>This is an excellent opportunity for experienced support workers seeking regular agency shifts within a specialist children's residential setting.</p> <p><strong>Apply today for immediate consideration.</strong></p>",
