   "description": "<p><strong>Residential Support Worker - Children's Residential</strong></p> <p><strong>Location:</strong> Birmingham - Yardley Wood, Kings Heath, Oldbury & Moseley<br><strong>Salary:</strong> £25,344 per annum &#43; £70 per sleep-in &#43; overtime<br><strong>Hours:</strong> 160 hours per month<br><strong>Contract:</strong> Full-Time, Permanent<br><strong>Essential: Full UK Driving Licence and NVQ 3 </strong></p> <p>Are you passionate about making a positive difference in the lives of children and young people?</p> <p>We are recruiting <strong>Residential Support Workers</strong> to join established <strong>Ofsted-registered children's residential homes</strong> across Birmingham.</p> <p>This is a fantastic opportunity for caring, reliable and resilient individuals who want to build a career within children's residential care.</p> <p><strong>The Role</strong></p> <p>As a Residential Support Worker, you will provide day-to-day care and support to children and young people, helping to create a safe, stable and nurturing home environment.</p> <p>Your responsibilities will include:</p> <ul> <li>Supporting and safeguarding children and young people</li><li>Building positive and professional relationships</li><li>Supporting young people with emotional and behavioural needs</li><li>Managing challenging behaviour and using appropriate de-escalation techniques</li><li>Following care plans, risk assessments and behaviour support plans</li><li>Supporting education, independence and daily living skills</li><li>Organising and participating in activities and community outings</li><li>Driving young people to school, appointments and activities</li><li>Completing accurate daily records and documentation</li><li>Working closely with colleagues, families and external professionals</li></ul> <p><strong>Hours & Pay</strong></p> <p>You will work <strong>160 contracted hours per month</strong>, which is approximately <strong>11 shifts per month</strong>.</p> <p>Shifts are typically <strong>8:00am-11:00pm</strong>, with working days varying according to the rota.</p> <p><strong>Sleep-ins are required</strong>, although the number will vary depending on the rota. Each sleep-in is paid at an additional <strong>£70</strong>.</p> <p>The <strong>£25,344 salary is the basic annual salary before sleep-in payments and overtime</strong>.</p> <p>Overtime is available, including opportunities to pick up additional shifts across the organisation's other homes.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
