   "description": "<p><b>Female Support Worker – Waking Nights | Sevenoaks</b></p> <p><strong>£25,845 per annum (pro rata) | Full-time – 39 hours per week</strong><br><strong>Waking Night Shifts: 10:00pm – 7:00am</strong></p> <p><strong>A full UK driving licence and access to your own vehicle are essential for this role to travel to and from shifts.</strong></p> <p><b>Make a Difference Every Night</b></p> <p>Looking for a career where every shift has a real impact? At Avenues, you'll support people to live the life they choose while building a rewarding career of your own.</p> <p>Whether you're already working in social care or looking for a meaningful career change, we'll provide all the training and support you need to succeed.</p> <p>At Avenues, people smile, laugh, grow and achieve together. We know that when our colleagues feel supported, valued and empowered, they help the people we support live happy, fulfilling lives.</p> <p><b>About the Role</b></p> <p>We're looking for caring and committed Female Support Workers to join our waking night team in Sevenoaks, supporting adults with learning disabilities, physical disabilities, epilepsy, communication needs and those receiving end-of-life care within a residential service.</p> <p>Located just a five-minute walk from Sevenoaks railway station, the service provides person-centred support in a safe and welcoming environment. During the night, you'll play a vital role in ensuring people feel safe, comfortable and well supported, responding to individual needs while promoting dignity and independence.</p> <p><b>What You'll Be Doing</b></p> <p>No two nights are the same. Your role will include:</p> <ul> <li>Providing reassurance and support throughout the night</li><li>Completing regular wellbeing and safety checks in line with individual support plans</li><li>Supporting with personal care in a respectful and dignified manner where required</li><li>Responding calmly and appropriately to any overnight needs or emergencies</li><li>Completing accurate records and handovers to ensure continuity of care</li><li>Helping maintain a safe, clean and comfortable home environment</li><li>Working closely with colleagues to provide high-quality, person-centred support</li></ul> <p><b>No Experience? No Problem.</b></p> <p>If you're compassionate, reliable and eager to learn, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
