   "description": "<p><strong>HCSW - Band 3 (NHS Experience Essential)</strong></p> <p>At Cambridge University Hospitals (CUH), our values of<strong>Together, Safe, Kind and Excellent</strong> guide everything we do. We are seeking compassionate and experienced <strong>Healthcare Support Workers (HCSWs)</strong> committed to delivering high-quality patient care.</p> <p><strong>This vacancy is only open to applicants with current or previous NHS Healthcare Support Worker experience.</strong></p> <p>You will work alongside nurses, doctors and multidisciplinary teams to provide safe, effective and dignified care. Flexibility is required to work days, nights, weekends and bank holidays. Fixed shift patterns are not available.</p> Essential Requirements <p>Applicants must demonstrate:</p> <ul> <li>Previous NHS Healthcare Support Worker experience.</li> <li>Completion of an NHS-recognised National Care Certificate (NCC).</li> <li>Practical assessment against all 16 Care Certificate standards.</li> <li>Clinical competencies signed off in practice.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Please note:</strong> Online-only Care Certificate training is not accepted. Evidence of practical assessment and competency sign-off must be provided.</p> Required Competencies <ul> <li>Health and Safety</li> <li>Infection Prevention and Control / PPE</li> <li>Urinary catheter management and removal</li> <li>Vital signs monitoring and recording</li> <li>Manual blood pressure monitoring and recording</li> <li>Removal of an intravascular cannula</li> <li>Enhanced observations</li> </ul> Reapplication Clause <p>Applicants unsuccessful for a CUH Band 3 Healthcare Support Worker role within the last six months should not reapply, as applications will not be considered.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>This is a rewarding and hands-on role where you will make a real difference to patient care and experience.</p> <p>Full-time and part-time opportunities are available. Applicant must be able to work flexibly across a variety of shifts, including days, nights, weekends and bank holidays.</p> <p>Responsibilities include:</p> <ul> <li>Providing high-quality personal care.</li> <li>Supporting patients with eating and drinking.</li> <li>Undertaking and recording clinical observations, including blood pressure, pulse, temperature and urinalysis.</li> <li>Assisting patients with mobility.</li> <li>Supporting nurses and the multidisciplinary team in delivering patient care.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
